## 💻 How to Run Locally

Follow these steps to run the project on your local machine.

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/AllenVarghese167/Delivery_Delay_Prediction.git
```

```bash
cd Delivery_Delay_Prediction
```

### 2. Create a Virtual Environment

```bash
python -m venv venv
```

Activate the environment.

**Windows:**

```bash
venv\Scripts\activate
```

**macOS / Linux:**

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
```

### 3. Install Dependencies

```bash
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Run the Streamlit Application

```bash
python -m streamlit run app.py
```

### 5. Access the Application

Open the following URL in your browser:

```text
http://localhost:8501
```

The application allows users to enter delivery-related information and receive an estimated delivery time from the trained Linear Regression model.

---

## 🔮 Limitations and Future Improvements

### Limitations

- The model depends on the quality and availability of historical delivery data.
- Linear Regression assumes a linear relationship between input features and delivery time.
- Unexpected events such as traffic congestion and extreme weather may affect prediction accuracy.
- The dataset may not represent all real-world delivery scenarios.
- The model requires further validation before real-world business deployment.

### Future Improvements

- Compare Linear Regression with advanced regression algorithms.
- Explore Random Forest Regressor and Gradient Boosting Regressor.
- Perform hyperparameter optimization where applicable.
- Improve feature engineering using additional delivery-related variables.
- Integrate real-time traffic and weather information.
- Add model explainability using SHAP.
- Develop a dashboard for delivery performance monitoring.
- Implement automated model retraining.

